title HUNK82 — the query header: the typed clauses and their result count, above the narrowed shelf
prompt continue the recursion after HUNK81; take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first, self-approve, send as its own signed round to origin and xykj61, stop at custody gates
think HUNK79 drew the faceted search on glass yet the drawn page carried no word of WHAT was asked or HOW MANY were found — the shelf shows survivors but not the query nor the count. HUNK81's recommend and HUNK79's own next-line both named a query header the next crux. By Lindy-first crux-first it is the most durable next thing: a search-UX primitive reused across every search, pure painting, a clean no-drift property.
think Chose brushstroke/part_search_header.rye — format_query renders a parsed AndQuery back to a canonical space-separated key:value line, format_header assembles that (or the friendly `all parts`) plus an N-result(s) count from part_and.count_and, header_row draws a one-row anchor-palette grid, and search_screen stacks the header over HUNK79's and_search_shelf into one grid by HUNK53's cell-for-cell copy idiom.
think The crux is NO DRIFT: header and shelf both read the one typed line through the one parse_and — the header counts with count_and, the shelf filters with filter_and — so a header can never claim a count the shelf does not number. A sharper law makes the echo trustworthy: format_query renders a canonical line that RE-PARSES to the same query (parse_and(format_query(aq)) == aq), a fixed point of the parser like the sprite catalog and edit-list are of theirs — so the echo is the query the machine understood, not a transcript of keystrokes.
think Used a plain two-space gap and ASCII digits rather than a middle-dot separator — the skate glyph atlas is per-byte ASCII, so a multibyte U+00B7 would render as two garbage cells. Kept singular/plural (1 result vs N results) as a cheap correctness-and-pleasure branch.
obs GREEN on the first build. Proven on metal over four parts across four bands: material:stainless-304 max:100 reads `1 result`, an empty line `all parts  4 results`; a compound line's canonical render re-parses to the same query and equals the tidy single-spaced form; the header count equals and_search_result_count for every tested line; search_screen is cols wide and 1+rows tall, row 0 equal to header_row and the shelf region equal to and_search_shelf cell-for-cell, the header naming one result over hexnut's own row; the screen rasterizes to a lit canvas; a malformed clause refuses through the header before any shelf work (UnknownKey, NoColon), a zero/over-ceiling header refuses EmptyHeader/HeaderTooLarge, and an offset past the narrowed result refuses BadOffset.
obs A price is echoed as the keeper's own cents (canonical max:100, re-parseable) — a fact drawn for reading and compared, never a balance the tree can move (custody gate #3 untouched). No network, no key, no funds. TAME bans clean (not flagged by the scan), width exit 0; HUNK79 narrowed shelf and HUNK78 conjunction re-run GREEN beneath.
loom witness=hunk_part_search_header_witness parts=4 header_rows=1 screen_rows=5 fixed_point=canonical_query
